---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { donation } from '../lib/offers';
const support = donation();
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title={`About ${SITE.name}`} description={`${SITE.name} is a free, private photo metadata toolkit built by ${SITE.author}.`}>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top:32px">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={u('/')}>Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
      <p>{SITE.name} is a set of free tools to <strong>inspect, clean and analyze photo metadata</strong> without uploading photos anywhere.</p>
      <p>It’s built by <strong>{SITE.author}</strong>, an {SITE.authorBio.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + SITE.authorBio.slice(1)} Most online metadata tools upload your photos to a server to read them. That felt wrong for a privacy tool, so everything here runs on your own device.</p>
      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local first</strong>: photos are processed in your browser and never uploaded.</li>
        <li><strong>Lossless</strong>: removing metadata should never reduce image quality.</li>
        <li><strong>Plain language</strong>: explain what metadata means, not just list tag names.</li>
        <li><strong>Honest</strong>: metadata is evidence, not proof, and we say so.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Support this project</h2>
      <p>{SITE.name} is free and has no ads on the tools. It’s funded by a few clearly labelled <a href={u('/disclosure/')}>affiliate recommendations</a> and by our iPhone apps.{support && ' If it saved you time, you can also support it directly:'}</p>
      {support && (
        <p><a class:list={['btn btn-primary', { placeholder: !support.ready }]} href={support.ready ? support.url : '#'} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{support.label}</a></p>
      )}
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Feedback, bug reports and feature requests are welcome. Add your contact email or form here before launch.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
